  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-05T09:36:08.488Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I think it's a QoL addition to just include a button that enables us to hide the chat keyboard when we're texting our friends.\n\nWe need this because while you can just look away/up from the keyboard in VR, desktop users cannot do that and have to stare at a virtual keyboard that fills up the entire screen. I think the keyboard showing up for desktop users may be a little counter-intuitive, because desktop users already have a physical keyboard in front of them and do not require a virtual one. I am not suggesting to make a permanent change, but I am asking if we can have a button or option to fold in the keyboard so we only see the text bar. This way, we can still look at our friends while typing things.",
